+### Viewing Redaction-Marked Environment Variables
 
-The `mise env` command provides flags to work with redacted variables:
+The `mise env` command provides flags to work with variables marked for
+redaction. These commands do not mask values; they select variables whose keys
+match redaction rules and print the selected raw values.
 
 ```bash
-# Show only redacted environment variables
+# Show assignments for variables marked for redaction. Values are not masked.
 mise env --redacted
 
 # Show only values (useful for piping)
 mise env --values
 
-# Show only values of redacted variables
+# Show only values of variables marked for redaction. Values are not masked.
 mise env --redacted --values
 ```
 
